<gpx version="1.1" creator="GPS Visualizer https://www.gpsvisualizer.com/" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1 http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1/gpx.xsd">
<wpt lat="29.375281" lon="-103.871939">
  <name>Banos de Madrid</name>
  <desc>Not a designated campsite, but a good area to consider setting-up camping. There is a decent chance there is water in Madrid Springs, but desert water sources are unpredictable and rangers will not be monitoring this water source for current conditions.(This water is often bitter from the tanins in the Cottonwood leaves)</desc>
  <sym>images/icon-1.png</sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="29.469013" lon="-103.95701">
  <name>Sauceda Bunkhouse</name>
  <desc>Consider booking a bed in the bunkhouse through Texas Parks and Wildlife. Sure you're only a couple days in, but it's a part of the experience. Running water available.</desc>
  <sym>images/icon-1.png</sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="29.557631" lon="-104.093688">
  <name>Terneros Creek Campsite</name>
  <desc>Not a designated campsite, but a good area to consider setting-up camping. There is a decent chance Terneros Creek has water, but desert water sources are unpredictable and rangers will not be monitoring this water source for current conditions.</desc>
  <sym>images/icon-1.png</sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="29.374514" lon="-103.873137">
  <name>Madrid House</name>
  <sym>images/icon-2.png</sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="29.481809" lon="-103.970436">
  <name>Cinco Tinajas</name>
  <sym>images/icon-2.png</sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="29.379719" lon="-103.884151">
  <name>Madrid Falls</name>
  <sym>images/icon-2.png</sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="29.501667" lon="-103.984417">
  <name>Junction Leyva Creek</name>
  <sym>images/icon-2.png</sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="29.393742" lon="-103.885153">
  <name>Mexicano Falls TH</name>
  <sym>images/icon-2.png</sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="29.214385" lon="-103.366487">
  <name>Homer Wilson Ranch</name>
  <desc>Not a designated campsite, but a good area to consider setting-up camping (at a legal distance from the trail and the ranchhouse itself). No water available to a water cache would have to be dropped in the available cache boxes while getting a National Park permit. </desc>
  <sym>images/icon-1.png</sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="29.265352" lon="-103.774468">
  <name>Maverick Campground</name>
  <sym>images/icon-1.png</sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="29.198666" lon="-103.604396">
  <name>Terlingua Abajo Campsites</name>
  <desc>Reserve a primitive car-camping site here when getting BBNP permits. There is a decent chance Terlingua Creek has water, but desert water sources are unpredictable and rangers will not be monitoring this water source for current conditions. You can consider driving-by to scout conditions prior to your trip, or as you get National Park permits</desc>
  <sym>images/icon-1.png</sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="29.212204" lon="-103.45722">
  <name>The Chimneys</name>
  <sym>images/icon-2.png</sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="29.241055" lon="-103.297256">
  <name>Boot Springs</name>
  <sym>images/icon-2.png</sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="29.21063" lon="-103.702892">
  <name>Tinaja Blanca</name>
  <desc>Shallows Tinajas may hold water depending on recent rains</desc>
  <sym>images/icon-2.png</sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="29.409754" lon="-103.903166">
  <name>Rock Art - Water</name>
  <desc>There is a large red anthropomorphic panel in an alcove above a pool that frequently holds water</desc>
  <sym>images/icon-2.png</sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="29.403523" lon="-103.887057">
  <name>Classic Mexicano Overlook</name>
  <desc>The view from 90% of photos of the waterfall</desc>
  <sym>images/icon-2.png</sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="29.377317" lon="-103.880968">
  <name>Chorro Spring</name>
  <desc>Follow a historic road to the pools and some of the best water in the park</desc>
  <sym>images/icon-2.png</sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="29.374286" lon="-103.854676">
  <name>Fresno Cascades</name>
  <desc>Some of the most reliable water in the park</desc>
  <sym>images/icon-2.png</sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="29.225146" lon="-103.301519">
  <name>South Rim</name>
  <desc>Site SW 4 is a good spot with great proximity to the South Rim.</desc>
  <sym>images/icon-1.png</sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="29.208569" lon="-103.699362">
  <name>Mesa de Anguila Campsite</name>
  <desc>Beautiful views into Mexico. Not a designated campsite, but a good area to consider setting-up camping. Tinajas on the Mesa are unpredictable sources of water and rangers will not be monitoring this water source for current conditions.</desc>
  <sym>images/icon-1.png</sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="29.269902" lon="-103.757337">
  <name>Barton Warnock Visitor Center</name>
  <sym>images/icon-2.png</sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="29.664173" lon="-104.117658">
  <name>Casa Piedra Trailhead Start</name>
  <sym>images/icon-2.png</sym>
</wpt>
<wpt lat="29.267853" lon="-103.302808">
  <name>Chisos Basin Finish</name>
  <sym>images/icon-2.png</sym>
</wpt>
